  "overview": "**Asphalt** is a light-first design system anchored on `#ffffff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#0d6efd` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `System UI` (120px display down to 16px body), unified by `.25rem` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **GO-JEK**. Source: live stylesheet extraction (https://asphalt.gojek.io/). Inventory: **80** colors, **10** typography steps, and **40** documented components (all rights reserved license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 40 component tokens with documented paddings: `.375rem .75rem`, `.35em .65em`, `.5rem 1rem`, `.375rem 2.25rem .375rem .75rem`, `1rem 1rem`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#ffffff` cards; separate sibling sections using `#e8e8e8` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 .5rem 1rem rgba(0,0,0,.15)`, `0px 0px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06)`) paired with `#e8e8e8` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#0d6efd` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#ffffff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#0d6efd` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.2:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `System UI` headings with `System UI` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `.25rem` base geometry across inputs and buttons (.25rem on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#ffffff` surface shifts and `#e8e8e8` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `.25rem` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `form-check-input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
